[node name="Human Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 496.0
offset_top = 171.0
offset_right = 1135.0
offset_bottom = 596.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "     Despite hailing primarily from Tyber & the Rimansse, Humans are ubiquitous across the world. A 
proven combination of tenacity, ambition, and fool-hardiness has enmeshed Humans into every 
cultural hotspot and backwater village. Such diversity has given Humans a unique outlook on life
and where it may lead them.
     Other races tend to view Humans on the whole as short-sighted and a touch arrogant. Elves, in
particular, see Humans as a meddlesome and prideful bunch. A war between the Human Kingdom of
Tyber and The Elvish King Ari'Akai was fought in recent memory. Though it ended in near stalemate,
the Elves remain embittered.
     Dwarves and Gnomes harbor no such blood feud and enjoy an opportunistic relationship with
the Human Kingdoms. Foodstuffs and precious earths are of undeniable value and are happily 
exchanged when a mutually beneficial arrangement can be made. Gnomes, in particular, enjoy
collaboration with those Humans fortunate enough to wield magic. Many an arcane breakthrough
has been achieved by this union of mental ingenuity.
     Halflings are happily integrated into Human civilization. A shared joy of singing, dancing, ribald
jokes, enebriation, and general hullabaloo made the races fast friends eons ago. Nowadays it is
rare to find a group of Human travelers without a Halfling or two in tow. Such companionship has 
mixed their oral histories so thouroughly that nearly every folk hero of one has a mirror on the other
side. "

[node name="Human Bonuses" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
