[node name="Half-Elf Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 496.0
offset_top = 171.0
offset_right = 1135.0
offset_bottom = 596.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "     A blend of Human and Elf, Half-Elves are a robust athletic and handsome people. Phenotypically 
they resemble Humans more than Elves, but a study of the face and build reveal the fairer race. This 
Human lean applies to their life-span as well. 160 years may be two lifespans by Human standards,
but it pales to the 450 years of the Elf. In general, a Half-Elf has the curiosity, inventiveness, 
and ambition of Human ancestry, and the refined senses, love of nature, and artistic tastes of 
Elven ancestry.
     Due to the protracted conflict between Elves and Humans, much is assumed of a Half-Elf by the
very nature of his/her existence. Having no exclusive settlements of their own, Half-Elves are found
living amongst Elves and Humans. They are often familially estranged and put-down due to
whichever half of them their neighbors are not. This leads many a Half-Elf to a life of wander.
     This lack of community tends to make Half-Elves self sufficient and mild mannered. Vocal Half-
Elves have seen how easily attention can turn to persecution and most are happy to live light and
move on when the wind begins to blow against them. For this reason, Half-Elves take friendship
very seriously. Unused to benefit of the doubt, displays of kindness strike them deeply.
     It is with Dwarves, Gnomes, and Halflings that Half-Elves are most at ease. Without overarching
cultural expectations, Half-Elves are able to relinquish the defenses so often needed among their
half kindred. Though such company provides a nice reprise, most Half-Elves hold on to a hope that 
one day they may prove themselves to their original community."

[node name="Half-Elf Bonuses" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 24.0
offset_top = 334.0
offset_right = 465.0
offset_bottom = 623.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "Though Half-Elves gain no Bonus Stats, they do enjoy other Benefits:

-- 30% Resistance to Sleep Spells

-- 30% Resistance to Charm Spells

-- 60ft of Infravsion

-- +2 on Observation rolls

-- Proficiency in One of: Hunting, Herbalism, Fishing, Direction Sense"

[node name="Gnome Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 481.0
offset_top = 144.0
offset_right = 1136.0
offset_bottom = 596.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "     Slightly shorter and a bit less stocky than Dwarves, Gnomes are a peculiar and somewhat vanishing 
race. Often deeply mired in a passionate pursuit, it is uncommon to find a Gnome whiling away the
hours in a common room or village green. This is not to say that Gnomes are inherently unsocial but
rather that a Gnome rarely affords itself time to gossip and fraternize.
     Originally of the Underdark, the Gnomish race grew alongside the Dwarves. There, in the deep 
ravines beneath the mountains, the two became certain and inseparable allies. Gnomes and Dwarves 
are now nearly fraternal in interaction; each quick to adopt their traditional role when trouble arises.
     For the Gnome's part, this meant ingenuity. As Dwarves are unable to interact with magic, the 
responsibility of teasing apart the arcane fell to the Gnomes. Such a devotion left an indelible mark 
and the creativity required to craft magical components bled into other scholarly pursuits.
     From engineering aqueducts and elevators to classifying and codifying various crystalline 
structures, Gnomes have authored countless detailed manuscripts. Gnomish culture has evolved to 
encourage such endeavors and prominent familial lines are backed by volume after volume of 
academic toil. Those without such pedigree can be found far afield, working with single-minded fervor 
to publish original findings.
     Such abstract work requires a life divorced from the everyday labors of crop cultivation and the 
gathering of timber. Therefore Gnomes are nearly always found in metropolitan areas. Places of 
stability, where rare components can be ordered and collaborative research quickly couriered by 
like-minds, are where Gnomes thrive. For Gnomes whom are able to achieve these works, their 
brilliance, and the wealth that comes alongside it, is welcomed most anywhere in the world."

[node name="Gnome Bonuses" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 18.0
offset_top = 326.0
offset_right = 456.0
offset_bottom = 631.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "Bonus Scores and Abilities include:

-- +1 Intelligence, -1 Wisdom

-- 60ft of Infravision

--Proficiency in Reading/Writing

--Proficiency in one of  Gem-Cutting, Appraisal, Engineering

-- One Extra Use of any Magical Item with Charges

--25% to Identify Magical Scroll if not Magic-User
   Extra 25% if Magic-User"

[node name="Elf Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 482.0
offset_top = 142.0
offset_right = 1131.0
offset_bottom = 601.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "     With high cheek bones, pointed ears and vulpine jawlines, the visage of an Elf is unmistakable. 
Longer-lived than any other race, often by hundreds of years, Elves are the keepers of history; 
and therefore, the keepers of the world's collective conscience. No other race can reach back through 
time and recall the mistakes of past civilizations. The Elves alone are certain that, in a past eon, the 
world was different. The forests were deeper. The wildlife reasoned. The air hummed with magic. 
Something undefinable was lost and every Elf seems to carry that memory forward, wary that it may 
erode further.
     To the other races, this makes Elves appear standoffish, as if their mind is preoccupied; engaged in 
an inner dialogue with itself. Humans are not afraid to criticize this haughty and superior behavior. 
The Elves meet this criticism, more often than not, with indifference. This indifference stretches to 
negotiations both business and hostile. Elves ever willing to wait for a more favorable circumstance or 
for the other party to finally see the wisdom of their argument. Such Elvish prudence easily resembles 
stubbornness.
     Though Elvish merchants do not command the largest fleets and Elvish cities do not boast the 
greatest populations, Elves control the majority of the world's most powerful places and institutions. 
Here too, their prudence can just as easily be interpreted as inaction. Critics declare Elvish leadership 
that of a caretaker, rather than that of a visionary.
     Elvish mystique does still run strong and Elves command inherent respect most anywhere they go. 
Elves are near universally well-educated, well-mannered, and articulate to the layman. Internal Elvish 
culture demands such standards and it doesn't hurt that most Elves are nearing 60 before they make 
an independent life for themselves."

