[node name="Dwarf Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 474.0
offset_top = 131.0
offset_right = 1134.0
offset_bottom = 590.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_gdq3k")
text = "     Tireless, and hardy, the average Dwarf makes their living on honest tasks of definite value. Whether 
it's slabs from a quarry, timber from a logging camp, or metal goods hammered from fired ore, a Dwarf 
finds comfort that his/her work affects the world with visual certainty. This is not to say that their work 
is crude, on the contrary, crafted Dwarven goods and material tend to be of the highest quality and 
Dwarves make certain that such quality is properly compensated.
     Dwarves hail from deep underground in the Underdark. Their history is replete with the warfare that 
such dangerous origins necessitate. A warrior's ethic is celebrated culture-wide and tales of valor 
dominate Dwarven folklore. In battle, a Dwarf will rarely flee, and a company of Dwarves will fall to a 
man, even if the odds against it are insurmountable. This quality of fighter, combined with the 
exceptional quality of their arms and armaments, make a Dwarven legion one of the most formidable 
units that can be fielded in a battle.
     Dwarves are also a long-lived race. With many Dwarves reaching ages of 250 before succumbing to 
old age. Their stout and stocky builds keep them in good health, and even an aged Dwarf makes for a 
sturdy soldier deep into his/her twilight years. There are many myths that this unnatural strength stems 
from a magical property innate in a Dwarf's biology, and though nothing has been proven, it is well 
known that Dwarves cannot access the arcane. Perhaps such prohibition from magic is the Dwarf's 
payment for the many benefits they otherwise enjoy.
     Dwarves show no resentment towards this limitation, they have forged strong bonds with Gnomes 
whom they trust with whatever magical discoveries are made in the Underdark. To the other races, 
Dwarves are a known entity; dour, taciturn, a hard laborer, a shrewd barter, and a tough scrap. 
To Dwarves, the other races are worthy of suspicion, until proven otherwise."

[node name="Dwarf Bonuses" type="Label" parent="."]
